 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The Prophet ﷺ is addressed in 99:10-15, 101:1 and 102:10-15: no motif there. Allah's first-person «أوجبناه على أنفسنا» (As-Sa'di) and «ننجيك» (Al-Muyassar) are not used. Geometric for «ولو شاء ربك», light for «بإذن الله» and «ننج المؤمنين» (after «رسلنا»), stars for the heavens, an hourglass for «فهل ينتظرون». STAGING v4: c1 (99-100) stays ambient (geometric): Allah's will and permission, and 99:10-15 is addressed to the Prophet ﷺ about his own conduct (would you compel people): params.quiet over 99:10-15; the light plate on by the permission of Allah (100:7) is replaced by a geometric one (a light plate never starts on an attribute of Allah). c2 (101-102): the people told to look (Al-Muyassar: the Prophet's ﷺ people), three faceless men in dark robes in a town at night, under the night sky; the command to look is not acted by them (a command to others is never shown as done): the camera tilts up to the heavens (101:5) and down to the earth (101:6); the camera on them for a people who do not believe (101:12; no gesture inside the negation); an hourglass for do they wait (102:2-9; the days of the earlier nations are not drawn). 102:10-15 is the Prophet's ﷺ answer: nobody speaks or turns toward an empty side, the camera only (on them for wait, 102:11, then wide). c3 (103) stays ambient (dawn): Allah's promise to save His messengers and the believers, in His own words; the messengers (of different eras) are not drawn and no group of believers is staged (Al-Muyassar applies it to the Prophet ﷺ and his followers, who are never shown); params.quiet over all of 103; the light plate starts on 103:6, not on a word for Allah."
